Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R):<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Assertion&nbsp;(A):</strong></td><td>At a sink temperature of <span class="math-tex">\(-273^{\circ}\)</span>&nbsp;C, the efficiency of a Carnot engine will be 1.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason&nbsp;(R):</strong></td><td>The efficiency of a Carnot engine is given by&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\(\eta=1-{{T_{\sin k}}\over{T_{source}}}\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table><br>In the light of the above statements choose the correct answer from the options given below:<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are true and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are true but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is not the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is true but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is false.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is false but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is true.</td></tr></tbody></table>

Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I:</strong> </span></td><td style="text-align: justify;"><span id="cke_bm_1911S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>The efficiency of any thermodynamic engine can approach <span class="math-tex">\(100\%\)</span> if friction and all dissipative processes are reduced.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td style="text-align: justify;">The first law of thermodynamics is applicable only to non-living systems.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 6%;">1.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect and <strong>Statement II</strong> is correct.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">2.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and<strong> Statement II</strong> are correct.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">3.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I</strong> and <strong>Statement II</strong> are incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">4.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct and <strong>Statement II</strong> is incorrect.</td></tr></tbody></table>
